From: TechNet <local>
Subject: [PATCH] rotation-manager: Keep a locked orientation on the lock screen

On phones the lock screen is forced to portrait when the shell locks and
the previous transform is put back on unlock. With the orientation lock
on, whoever set it has said which way the panel goes -- on Thor that is
the keyboard dock, which holds the phone in landscape -- so leave the
transform alone in both directions. Without this the docked phone turns
portrait every time it locks, and the unlock path, which cannot match
the sensor while the orientation is locked, resets it a second time.

--- a/src/rotation-manager.c
+++ b/src/rotation-manager.c
@@ -258,6 +258,12 @@ fixup_lockscreen_orientation (PhoshRotationManager *self, gboolean lock)
   if (!self->monitor)
     return;
 
+  /* A locked orientation holds on the lock screen too */
+  if (self->orientation_locked) {
+    self->prelock_transform = -1;
+    return;
+  }
+
   /* Only bother on phones */
   if (!is_phone (self))
     return;
